# Everything here is produced by a probe and rebuilt by the next one; nothing
# in this list is an input. The repro deliberately writes its artifacts next to
# the shader, because "which files did the run write?" IS the measurement (see
# dep4723.py), so without this the directory fills with stale depfiles and
# preprocessed output -- and a stale .d is indistinguishable from one the run
# under test produced, which is precisely the trap this issue is about.
*.d
*.i
*.dxo
history-work/

# Left by probing the pre-v1.7.2212 spelling of -P, which took the output
# filename as a value: `-P -Fi x.i` on such a release writes to a file called
# `-Fi`. measure-history.py cleans it up; this is belt and braces.
-Fi
